
1. Setup 
bash
cd backend
python -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate      # Windows: venv\Scripts\activate
pip install -r requirements.txt

2. Set the two secrets (new step — the ingestion key is new)
bash
export JWT_SECRET_KEY="any-long-random-string"
export INGESTION_API_KEY="any-other-long-random-string"

If skipped, both fall back to placeholder defaults in the code — fine for local testing, but the tester should know these exist.

3. Seed and run 
bash
python seed.py
uvicorn main:app --reload --port 8000

4. Test the previously-existing stuff 
Public endpoint, no auth:

bash
curl http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/events

Admin login:

bash
curl -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/auth/login \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"username": "admin", "password": "ChangeMe123!"}'

Admin endpoint with the returned token:

bash
curl http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/admin/events \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer PASTE_TOKEN_HERE"

5. Test the new part — ingestion endpoint

Without a key (should return 401):

bash
curl -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/internal/events \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"event_type":"Flood","city":"Pune","state":"Maharashtra","latitude":18.5204,"longitude":73.8567,"severity":"High","confidence_score":92,"timestamp":"2026-09-14T10:00:00"}'

With the correct key (should return 201 and the created event):

bash
curl -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/internal/events \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -H "X-API-Key: any-other-long-random-string" \
  -d '{"event_type":"Flood","city":"Pune","state":"Maharashtra","latitude":18.5204,"longitude":73.8567,"severity":"High","confidence_score":92,"timestamp":"2026-09-14T10:00:00"}'

Then confirm it shows up publicly:

bash
curl http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/events

Easiest way to test everything at once: 
just go to http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs after starting the server —
Swagger UI lists every route including /internal/events, and you can click "Try it out" on each one instead of writing curl commands by hand.
